        "name": "Gridkin fixture — far-node WHERE",
        "description": "A two-hop tree that separates the WHERE-matching far node reached by the RIGHT edge type from a decoy reached by the WRONG one. Root A -PG_LINKS-> mid B; B fans out three ways: -PG_LINKS-> C1 (kind=tail, the true match), -PG_LINKS-> C2 (kind=mid, filtered out), and -PG_OPTIONAL-> C3 (kind=tail, a decoy on the wrong edge type). A predicate on the far node `c` of a `(a)-[:PG_LINKS]->(b)-[:PG_LINKS]->(c)` chain must land on the structural far node only — it must never leak onto C3. Regression fixture for the deferred multi-hop far-node-WHERE duplicate-join defect.",
